{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have reviewed the gate report and the application files. The report identifies a single issue: several figure briefs for overview figures (FIG. 1 and FIG. 2) describe numbered parts as \"unnumbered,\" which creates an internal inconsistency. I will correct these briefs to refer to all numbered parts by their assigned names and numerals, ensuring consistency with the numeral list, the detailed description, and the briefs for the detail views.\n\nHere are the changes I will make:\n\n1.  **`figures/FIG-1.md`**: I will update the description of the removable thermal module to correctly identify the mating channel (52).\n2.  **`figures/FIG-2.md`**: I will update this brief to correctly identify multiple parts that were previously described as \"unnumbered.\" This includes the shell floor (12), removable absorbent wick (72), ledges (18), mechanical exposure indicator (80), downward guide ducts (48), peripheral outlet openings (50), compressible lid gasket (64), depending indexing rib (62), mating channel (52), and the central inlet opening (46).\n\nThese changes will resolve all findings from the gate report by ensuring that all parts are referred to consistently throughout the application. No changes are needed for any other files."}
